  "profile": {
    "video_id": "iron-snail:_knrP8B7IeY",
    "purpose": "A lightning-round showcase of 24 mostly thrifted and vintage fall clothing pieces. It is filmed as Michael walks to his favourite trails on his last day before moving from New York to Portland, Maine. It also previews the first Iron Snail knitwear piece, the Billy Goat sweater.",
    "video_type": "other",
    "thesis": "A personal roundup of favourite fall pieces (vests, sweaters, field coats, pants, shirts, denim jackets and suede) bought thrifted, on eBay or new. Each gets a quick note on fit, quality and value, framed by a farewell to New York and the reveal of the Iron Snail Billy Goat sweater.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "The video covers 24 fall pieces, including vests, cardigans, sweaters, field coats, pleated pants, overshirts and several denim and suede jackets.",
      "Michael and Taylor are moving from New York to Portland, Maine; the video is filmed on his last day at favourite trail spots.",
      "The first Iron Snail knitwear piece, the Billy Goat, is made of 100% Targhee wool, chosen to balance durability with softness compared with Merino.",
      "Some pieces are flagged as misses: a GAP collared sweater that is too small, a slouchy Inis Meáin knit, an SEH Kelly SB jacket that doesn't fit, and a Boy Scouts overshirt.",
      "Filson quality is praised, but its pricing strategy makes the brand hard to recommend unless bought on sale.",
      "Denim highlights include a Ralph Lauren blanket-lined jacket, a modified Tuf Nut type II jacket, an Imogene + Willie Sawtooth overshirt and a made-in-Canada Carhartt blanket-lined jacket.",
      "The Prologue Denim Jacket will get a companion jacket in the coming year, and Iron Snail jeans production is coming soon.",
      "Sponsor: Vaer G2 Meridian GMT watch."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Fall fashion essentials",
        "summary": "A teaser montage of highlight pieces (Carhartt jacket, Ralph Lauren pants, Inis Meáin knit, suede jacket, SEH Kelly coat, Billy Goat sweater) and the intro to the 24-piece lightning round.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 0
      },
      {
        "title": "Moving news and trails",
        "summary": "Michael reveals that he and Taylor are leaving New York for Portland, Maine, and sets up the video as a walk to his favourite trails.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Thrifty clothing review",
        "summary": "Covers a Field Master suede vest, a New Zealand Shetland wool knit vest, an early Columbia cardigan, a Lido ski sweater, a GAP collared sweater that's too small and an Inis Meáin silk-alpaca knit.",
        "first_segment": 2,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "Vaer watch partnership",
        "summary": "Sponsor read explaining how the Vaer G2 Meridian GMT watch tracks three time zones.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Iron snail knitting",
        "summary": "Introduces the Billy Goat, the first Iron Snail knitwear piece, made from 100% Targhee wool. Explains the breed's history and why its wool is more durable and springier than Merino.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Vintage field coats",
        "summary": "Covers SEH Kelly pieces lost or delayed in shipping (Balcamaan, SB jacket modelled by Taylor) and a 1950s-60s vintage field coat with fit and collar issues.",
        "first_segment": 8,
        "last_segment": 10
      },
      {
        "title": "Apparel brand spotlight",
        "summary": "Covers Ralph Lauren Andrew pleated pants, a BRUT sweatshirt, a Lady White sweatshirt and the Taylor Stitch Division shirt. Also discusses two Filson jackets and Filson's sale-driven pricing.",
        "first_segment": 10,
        "last_segment": 12
      },
      {
        "title": "Denim and work shirts",
        "summary": "Covers vintage Levi's 501s, a Ralph Lauren blanket-lined denim jacket, a modified Tuf Nut jacket, a Boy Scouts wool overshirt, an Imogene + Willie Sawtooth overshirt, a Lee Storm Rider and a made-in-Canada Carhartt jacket.",
        "first_segment": 13,
        "last_segment": 15
      },
      {
        "title": "Final New York goodbye",
        "summary": "At his last favourite spot, Michael shows the final piece, a Canadian-made Mountain Goat suede jacket, then says goodbye to New York.",
        "first_segment": 16,
        "last_segment": 17
      }
    ],
